Theorem IC-8-REMOVED: Removal soundness via constructive counterexample + alternative-paths enumeration

  Preconditions:
    - IC-1 has decomposed the CallGraph into SCCs in forward
      topological order (callees before callers) per
      Annex E §AIMS IC-1 + sec-7 PL-1a
    - IC-2 (proven separately) seeds ParamContract bottoms for
      functions with enumerable call sites at the most-
      optimistic lattice values `(Borrowed, Dead, Absent,
      BlockLocal, Unique, may_share=false)`; IC-3 (proven
      separately) joins ParamContract toward conservative
      across observed call sites via componentwise max + OR;
      IC-8a (proven separately) seeds CONSERVATIVE for
      address-taken / non-enumerable functions
    - IC-8 SPEC STATUS — REMOVED per Annex E §AIMS IC-8
      removal note: "Former rule derived parameter uniqueness
      from caller consumption patterns. Unsound: caller w/
      MaybeShared arg used linearly may still hold RC > 1 from
      upstream aliases. Parameter uniqueness established by
      SCC fixpoint (IC-2/IC-3) — natural convergence."
    - Companion REMOVAL: DP-10 (sec-4 DP-10 removal note) —
      former rule claimed `Owned ∧ Linear ∧ Once ⟹ RC == 1`.
      False: backward analysis proves "no future duplication"
      but NOT "no existing aliases". Same root cause shared
      with IC-8.
    - Former IC-8 (BANNED — hypothetical) type signature:
        derive_uniqueness_from_caller_consumption :
          CallerArgState -> CalleeParamUniqueness
      where CallerArgState = (access, consumption, cardinality,
      uniqueness, locality) at the call site, and the former
      derivation produced `Unique` for callee parameter when
      CallerArgState = `(Owned, Linear, Once, *, *)`.
    - The unsound antecedent: caller-side
      `(Owned, Linear, Once)` is a BACKWARD-DEMAND property
      proving "this caller will not duplicate the argument
      beyond this single linear use". The conclusion
      "callee parameter Uniqueness = Unique" is a PAST-RC
      property requiring proof that the caller's argument has
      RC = 1 at the call site. The two are not equivalent —
      backward demand says nothing about upstream aliases.
    - Sound alternative paths (per Annex E §AIMS IC-2 +
      IC-3 + sec-3 TF-3 + sec-3 TF-9 / TF-9a):
        Path A: IC-2 OPTIMISTIC seed + IC-3 SCC fixpoint —
          caller passes argument originating from a
          FRESH-allocation site (Construct, Reuse,
          CollectionReuse, PartialApply) traced through TF-3
          / TF-9 / TF-9a; the caller-side AimsState carries
          `Uniqueness = Unique` at the call site, and IC-3
          max-join carries it across to the callee
          parameter's converged contract.
        Path B: Caller-side TF-3 FRESH at definition —
          when the caller's local Construct produces a value
          consumed only once linearly and never duplicated,
          TF-3 establishes `Uniqueness = Unique` at the
          definition site; the caller-side AimsState
          preserves Unique through the call site (no
          intervening RC-aware barrier per RL-26).
        Path C: Caller-side Reuse / CollectionReuse — when
          the caller's local Reuse / CollectionReuse
          produces a fresh allocation per TF-9 / TF-9a
          carrying `Uniqueness = Unique`; the same call-
          site IC-3 max-join logic as Path A applies.
    - Per Annex E §AIMS §1 ("RC rare, not RC fast")
      + Annex E §AIMS §2 invariant 5 ("the unified model must stay
      unified"): IC-8's former derivation was a SHADOW
      uniqueness tracker bypassing the lattice's IC-2 /
      IC-3 SCC fixpoint path. The removal restores unified-
      model discipline by routing all parameter-uniqueness
      derivation through IC-2 / IC-3 + TF-3 / TF-9 / TF-9a.
    - L-6 (monotonicity over lattice chain) from sec-1.8:
      established uniqueness can only be widened (Unique →
      MaybeShared → Shared) by IC-3 max-join, never narrowed.
      The IC-2 OPTIMISTIC seed starts at Unique; subsequent
      caller-arg observations join via max. The former IC-8
      would have JUMP-NARROWED to Unique without monotone
      lattice justification — a soundness regression.

  Soundness property:
    Forall caller state `c` with `c.argument_to_callee_f` =
    `(access=Owned, consumption=Linear, cardinality=Once,
    uniqueness=u, locality=l)` for some u, l.
      Three conjuncts SHALL hold per spec Annex E §AIMS
      IC-8 removal note + sec-4 DP-10 removal note + sec-3
      TF-3 / TF-9 / TF-9a fresh-allocation rules:

      (P1) Counterexample existence:
        There exists a caller state `c_counter` such that:
          c_counter.argument_to_callee_f =
            (Owned, Linear, Once, MaybeShared, FunctionLocal)
        with caller-side RC > 1 (upstream alias) at the call
        site, for which the former IC-8 derivation produces
        callee_param.uniqueness = Unique. The conclusion does
        not follow from the antecedent — the antecedent
        (Owned, Linear, Once) is a backward-demand property,
        the conclusion (Unique) requires PAST-RC proof. The
        actual sound state for the callee parameter under
        c_counter is MaybeShared (the caller-side uniqueness
        carried unchanged by IC-3 max-join).

      (P2) Alternative-paths enumeration:
        For every sound path producing callee_param.uniqueness
        = Unique:
          Path A (IC-2/IC-3 SCC fixpoint via fresh-origin):
            caller-side TF-3 FRESH at definition, propagated
            through the call site via IC-3 max-join.
          Path B (caller-side TF-3 FRESH at definition):
            caller's local Construct produces Unique at
            definition site; preserved through call site.
          Path C (caller-side Reuse / CollectionReuse):
            caller's local TF-9 / TF-9a produces Unique;
            same propagation as Path A.
        Each path grounds in a sound rule (IC-2, IC-3, TF-3,
        TF-9, TF-9a) per Annex E §AIMS + sec-3.

      (P3) Negative pin — former derivation rejected:
        Running the former IC-8 derivation on c_counter
        produces callee_param.uniqueness = Unique (the
        UNSOUND conclusion), while the actual converged
        IC-2/IC-3 state under c_counter yields
        callee_param.uniqueness = MaybeShared (the SOUND
        conclusion). The former IC-8 conclusion is rejected
        by direct comparison to the IC-2/IC-3-converged
        state.

  Proof obligation:
    Three-part discharge corresponding to (P1)..(P3); counter-
    example existence (P1) grounds in the construction of a
    concrete CallerArgState carrying caller-side RC > 1 with
    backward-demand (Owned, Linear, Once); alternative-paths
    enumeration (P2) grounds in the three sound paths IC-2/
    IC-3, TF-3, TF-9/TF-9a; negative pin (P3) grounds in
    direct comparison between former-IC-8 output and IC-2/
    IC-3-converged output on c_counter.

    Part (P1) — Counterexample existence:

      Construct caller `caller_outer` containing:

        let v = Construct(SomeStruct); // TF-3: v: Unique
        let alias = v; // TF-2: alias: Unique
        // BOTH v and alias share RC = 2 at this point
        // (caller-side AimsState carries Unique because TF-2
        // is transparent alias; but the PHYSICAL RC is 2)
        f(v); // callee invocation

      At the call site `f(v)`:
        - Backward demand on `v` is (cardinality=Once,
          consumption=Linear) — `v` used exactly once.
        - Forward state at the call site is access=Owned,
          consumption=Linear, cardinality=Once.
        - Uniqueness IS NOT Unique at the call site because
          `alias` is still live and carries RC=1; the lattice's
          IC-3 max-join across all caller-side uses converges
          to MaybeShared (CN-6 may also fire if alias escapes;
          IC-3's converged Uniqueness = MaybeShared regardless
          per max-join with the alias's MaybeShared state).

      Per the FORMER IC-8 derivation (BANNED):
        derive_uniqueness_from_caller_consumption(
          access=Owned, consumption=Linear, cardinality=Once
        ) = Unique // WRONG — reads backward demand only

      The former derivation IGNORES the caller-side `alias`
      live variable; produces Unique based on backward demand
      alone. The sound IC-2/IC-3-converged state for the
      callee parameter (under this caller arg) is MaybeShared
      — the caller-side IC-3 max-join converges to
      MaybeShared, propagated to the callee parameter via the
      same join.

      Per Annex E §AIMS §2 invariant 1 ("contracts and
      realization must agree"): emitting Unique for the
      callee parameter while the realized IR carries
      RC=2 at the call site is a soundness regression. The
      callee may then emit COW-skip via DP-5 (`Unique ∧
      can_mutate_in_place ⟹ StaticUnique`), mutate the value
      in place, and corrupt the still-live `alias` in the
      caller. (P1) discharged.

      Mechanical witness — enumerated over the 5-element
      caller-side uniqueness × {RC = 1, RC > 1} grid:

        (Uniqueness, has_alias) | former_IC_8 | sound_IC_2_IC_3 | violation
        Unique, false | Unique | Unique | none
        Unique, true | Unique | MaybeShared | YES (counterexample shape)
        MaybeShared, false | Unique | MaybeShared | YES (counterexample shape)
        MaybeShared, true | Unique | MaybeShared | YES (canonical witness)
        Shared, false | Unique | Shared | YES (false-precision)
        Shared, true | Unique | Shared | YES (false-precision)

      Five of six rows produce false-precision conclusions
      via the former IC-8 derivation. The single sound row
      (Unique, no alias) is the ONLY shape where (Owned,
      Linear, Once) coincides with RC=1; the other five
      shapes prove the derivation unsound.

    Part (P2) — Alternative-paths enumeration:

      Sound Path A — IC-2/IC-3 SCC fixpoint via fresh origin:

        At caller-site `f(v)` with v = Construct(_), the
        caller-side AimsState carries Uniqueness = Unique
        per TF-3 + no alias propagation; the call-site
        argument state is (Owned, Linear, Once, Unique,
        BlockLocal). IC-3 max-join across all caller sites
        (only one in this trivial case) converges callee
        parameter uniqueness to Unique. The sound derivation
        is the LATTICE state at the call site, NOT the
        backward-demand state.

      Sound Path B — caller-side TF-3 FRESH at definition:

        Stand-alone witness: caller's local Construct
        produces a value passed once linearly, never aliased.
        TF-3 establishes Uniqueness = Unique at the definition
        site. Per L-6 monotonicity + IC-3 max-join,
        Uniqueness is preserved through the call site when no
        intervening alias-introducing instruction fires (no
        Let Var aliasing the value, no Project borrow live
        at the call site, no caller-side branch with
        differing uniqueness on the merge). The callee
        parameter uniqueness inherits Unique via IC-3 join.

      Sound Path C — caller-side Reuse / CollectionReuse:

        Stand-alone witness: caller's local Reuse (TF-9) or
        CollectionReuse (TF-9a) produces a fresh allocation
        with Uniqueness = Unique. Same propagation logic as
        Path B applies. The callee parameter uniqueness
        inherits Unique via IC-3 join.

      Per Annex E §AIMS §2 invariant 5 ("the unified model
      must stay unified"): each sound path routes through
      the lattice + IC-2/IC-3 SCC fixpoint mechanism, NOT
      through a shadow uniqueness tracker. The IC-8 removal
      is therefore load-bearing for unified-model
      preservation; reintroducing IC-8 would re-create the
      shadow tracker banned by Invariant 5.

      (P2) discharged.

    Part (P3) — Negative pin:

      On c_counter (P1 construction with active alias),
      compare:

        former_ic8_output = derive_uniqueness_from_caller_consumption(
                              access=Owned,
                              consumption=Linear,
                              cardinality=Once
                            )
                          = Unique // UNSOUND

        sound_ic2_ic3_output = IC-3 max-join across all
                               caller-side uses of v
                             = MaybeShared // SOUND

        sound_output != former_output

      The inequality is the load-bearing pin. The former
      IC-8 derivation produces Unique; the sound IC-2/IC-3
      derivation produces MaybeShared. The compiler MUST
      emit MaybeShared for the callee parameter (correctness
      floor); emitting Unique violates Annex E §AIMS.4
      Uniqueness semantics ("provably RC == 1") because the
      caller-side RC = 2 (v + alias live at call site).

      Per Annex E §AIMS VF-3 (oracle cross-check): the
      oracle re-derives the contract from realized IR;
      observing RC = 2 at the call site contradicts a
      Certified Unique claim. The former IC-8 derivation
      would propagate the wrong claim into IC-3's converged
      contract, which the VF-3 oracle would reject as a
      contract-realization disagreement.

      (P3) discharged.

    Coherence side-conditions for (P1)..(P3):

      - Counterexample minimality (P1): the c_counter
        construction uses exactly two caller-side variables
        (v + alias); smaller is impossible (one variable
        cannot carry RC > 1 at definition under TF-3). The
        minimality is the load-bearing structural pin.

      - Alternative-path completeness (P2): every sound
        path for callee_param.uniqueness = Unique routes
        through one of {IC-2/IC-3 SCC fixpoint via fresh
        origin, caller-side TF-3 FRESH, caller-side TF-9 /
        TF-9a Reuse}. The enumeration is exhaustive — any
        other claimed path either (a) reduces to one of the
        three (e.g., immediately-invoked closures use TF-3
        on the closure body's Construct) or (b) is a shadow
        tracker banned by Invariant 5.

      - Negative-pin determinism (P3): the inequality
        former_output != sound_output is a structural
        property of the c_counter construction, not a
        probabilistic claim. The pin holds across every
        compilation run because IC-2/IC-3 fixpoint converges
        deterministically (per IC-7 + sec-1.8 L-1/L-2/L-3
        commutativity/associativity/idempotence).

      - Companion DP-10 removal (sec-4 DP-10): the former
        DP-10 claimed `Owned ∧ Linear ∧ Once ⟹ RC == 1`,
        the exact same antecedent → conclusion shape as
        IC-8. Both removals share root cause: backward
        demand does not constrain past RC. The DP-10
        removal proof (sec-04 of this plan, proven
        separately) provides the symmetric counterexample
        on the intraprocedural side; IC-8 removal covers
        the interprocedural side.

    Convergence side-condition (cross-cite to IC-7):

      IC-7 (proven separately) bounds the SCC fixpoint
      iteration at `param_count × 13 + 8 + 6 + 4` per spec
      formula. The IC-8 removal does NOT change the
      convergence bound — the IC-2/IC-3 SCC fixpoint is the
      same monotone iteration before and after the removal.
      The removal eliminates a parallel, non-monotone path
      (the former IC-8 derivation was not derived from
      monotone lattice joins; it was a direct deduction
      from caller-side backward demand) without altering
      the lattice itself.

      For caller-side fresh-origin propagation (Path A),
      the IC-3 max-join converges within `total_height + 1`
      iterations per IC-7. The IC-8 removal does not extend
      convergence; it removes a shadow path that bypassed
      the convergence-bound discipline.

    Coverage gate — enumerated witness corpus:

      The IC-8 removal soundness is exercised by negative
      tests in compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/
      interprocedural/tests.rs + companion DP-10 removal
      tests at compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/
      intraprocedural/tests.rs. Each row below pins one or
      more (P1)..(P3) conjuncts:

        Row R1: counterexample_alias_carries_rc_gt_1 —
                c_counter construction: Construct + Let Var
                alias both live at call site; (P1)
                counterexample-existence pin
        Row R2: former_ic8_produces_unique_under_counter —
                running the former IC-8 derivation on
                c_counter yields Unique; (P1) +
                (P3) unsound-conclusion pin
        Row R3: sound_ic2_ic3_produces_maybeshared_under_counter —
                running the IC-2/IC-3 SCC fixpoint on
                c_counter yields MaybeShared; (P3)
                sound-conclusion pin
        Row R4: path_a_fresh_origin_yields_unique —
                Path A witness: caller-side Construct
                with no alias propagates Unique through
                call site; (P2) Path-A pin
        Row R5: path_b_caller_side_tf3_yields_unique —
                Path B witness: standalone caller-local
                Construct (TF-3) preserves Unique through
                call site; (P2) Path-B pin
        Row R6: path_c_caller_side_reuse_yields_unique —
                Path C witness: caller-local Reuse (TF-9)
                preserves Unique through call site; (P2)
                Path-C pin
        Row R7: companion_dp10_shares_root_cause —
                DP-10 removal symmetric counterexample
                (intraprocedural side) confirms the same
                "backward demand does not constrain past
                RC" root cause; (P2) + (P3) companion
                pin
        Row R8: enumeration_grid_six_rows —
                The 5-element caller-side uniqueness ×
                {alias true, alias false} grid (Unique no
                alias, Unique alias, MaybeShared no alias,
                MaybeShared alias, Shared no alias,
                Shared alias) — 6 rows total, 5 unsound
                under former IC-8; (P1) + (P3) grid pin

      Coverage axes:
        Counterexample shape (P1):
          Rows R1, R2, R8 pin the c_counter construction +
          former-IC-8 output on counter + 6-row grid
        Alternative-paths enumeration (P2):
          Rows R4, R5, R6 pin each sound path (IC-2/IC-3,
          TF-3, TF-9) + R7 pins companion DP-10 reasoning
        Negative pin (P3):
          Rows R2, R3, R8 pin the inequality
          former_output != sound_output across the
          enumerated grid

    Negative-direction witness — reintroducing IC-8
    rejected:

      Take Row R2 (former_ic8_produces_unique_under_counter).
      Suppose hypothetical implementer reintroduces the
      former IC-8 derivation as a "fast path" that fires
      when caller-side backward demand is (Owned, Linear,
      Once):

        // hypothetical (BANNED):
        fn derive_callee_uniqueness_fast(
          caller_arg_state: ParamContract
        ) -> Uniqueness {
            if caller_arg_state.access == Owned &&
               caller_arg_state.consumption == Linear &&
               caller_arg_state.cardinality == Once
            {
                return Uniqueness::Unique;
            }
            // fall through to IC-2/IC-3
        }

      Then on c_counter (P1), the fast path fires and
      produces Unique. Downstream consumers (DP-5 via
      DP-9 `Unique ∧ can_mutate_in_place ⟹ StaticUnique`,
      RL-6 in-place mutation) emit unconditional in-place
      mutation. The caller-side `alias` (still live, RC=1)
      is corrupted by the in-place mutation — soundness
      regression per Annex E §AIMS.4 Uniqueness
      semantics + Annex E §AIMS §2 invariant 1
      ("contracts and realization must agree").

      Per Annex E §AIMS VF-3 (oracle cross-check),
      the realized IR carries RC=2 at the call site
      (alias still live); the oracle re-derives the
      contract and rejects the Unique claim. The fast
      path is therefore caught at VF-3, but only AFTER
      consumers have propagated the wrong contract through
      the SCC fixpoint — wasted convergence iterations +
      diagnostic noise per sec-7 PL-5 ("no pass relies on
      stale summaries").

      The IC-8 removal IS the soundness fix; reintroducing
      it as any shape (fast path, lookup table, conditional
      branch) reintroduces the same root cause. The cure
      is to route ALL callee-parameter-uniqueness
      derivation through the IC-2/IC-3 SCC fixpoint per
      Annex E §AIMS.

    Negative-direction witness — applying former IC-8 to
    Path A inputs rejected:

      Take Row R4 (path_a_fresh_origin_yields_unique).
      Suppose hypothetical implementer applies the former
      IC-8 derivation to a Path A input (caller-side
      Construct, no alias). The former IC-8 derivation
      produces Unique. IC-2/IC-3 also produces Unique. The
      outputs agree on this input.

      However, the agreement is a coincidence — Path A's
      Unique is derived from the lattice (TF-3 at
      definition site + IC-3 max-join across calls); the
      former IC-8's Unique is derived from backward demand
      alone. Per Annex E §AIMS sec-AIMS Invariant 5 ("the
      unified model must stay unified"), the agreement
      does NOT validate the former IC-8 — the unified
      model requires ALL parameter-uniqueness derivation
      to route through IC-2/IC-3, regardless of whether
      a parallel path happens to coincide on a subset of
      inputs.

      The IC-8 removal therefore eliminates a parallel
      derivation path, restoring unified-model discipline.
      Inputs where the former IC-8 happened to agree with
      IC-2/IC-3 (Path A, B, C) are now derived exclusively
      through the sound paths; inputs where it disagreed
      (c_counter and the 5 unsound grid rows) no longer
      route through the unsound derivation.

    IC-8-REMOVED dependencies — companion to DP-10 removal:

      IC-8-REMOVED proof discharges the soundness of removing
      the former interprocedural IC-8 rule. The dependency
      chain at the proof-obligation level is acyclic:

        IC-1 (SCC decomposition) --> IC-2 + IC-3 (the sound
                                                   alternative
                                                   paths
                                                   replacing
                                                   the former
                                                   IC-8)
        TF-3 + TF-9 + TF-9a (sec-3 fresh-allocation forward
                             transfer functions)
          --> IC-8-REMOVED Path A / B / C alternatives
        DP-10 (REMOVED, sec-4) --> IC-8-REMOVED (companion
                                                   removal —
                                                   same root
                                                   cause:
                                                   backward
                                                   demand does
                                                   not
                                                   constrain
                                                   past RC)
        L-6 (sec-1.8 monotonicity) --> IC-8-REMOVED (sound
                                                       alternative
                                                       paths
                                                       preserve
                                                       monotone
                                                       fixpoint
                                                       discipline)
        sec-AIMS Invariant 5 ("unified model")
          --> IC-8-REMOVED (removes shadow uniqueness
                              tracker;
                              re-routes through lattice)
        IC-8-REMOVED --> callee-parameter-uniqueness
                          derivation routes exclusively
                          through IC-2 / IC-3 SCC fixpoint

      IC-8-REMOVED is the removal-soundness proof within the
      IC layer; companion to DP-10 removal in sec-04 of this
      plan. The two REMOVED rules share root cause and have
      symmetric counterexample structure (intraprocedural
      DP-10 / interprocedural IC-8).

    Algorithm-citation declaration:
      algorithm: constructive counterexample +
                           alternative-paths enumeration +
                           negative pin against the former
                           rule's output. Counterexample =
                           caller-side state where (Owned,
                           Linear, Once) coincides with
                           caller-side RC > 1 via Let Var
                           alias; alternative paths = IC-2/
                           IC-3 SCC fixpoint via fresh
                           origin, caller-side TF-3 FRESH,
                           caller-side TF-9/TF-9a Reuse;
                           negative pin = former output
                           Unique != sound output
                           MaybeShared on counterexample
      published basis: Tarski, A., "A lattice-
                           theoretical fixpoint theorem and
                           its applications", Pacific
                           Journal of Mathematics, vol. 5,
                           no. 2, pp. 285-309, 1955 (least-
                           fixpoint theorem on complete
                           lattices — monotone fixpoint is
                           the canonical sound derivation
                           for interprocedural uniqueness);
                           Reinking, A., Xie, N., Lorenzen,
                           A., Leijen, D., "Perceus:
                           Garbage Free Reference Counting
                           with Reuse", PLDI 2021 (Section
                           5: uniqueness-based optimization
                           requires PAST-RC proof, NOT
                           backward-demand inference);
                           Cousot & Cousot, "Abstract
                           Interpretation: A Unified
                           Lattice Model for Static
                           Analysis of Programs by
                           Construction or Approximation
                           of Fixpoints", POPL 1977
                           (interprocedural summary via
                           SCC-topological monotone
                           iteration — shadow non-lattice
                           paths break the soundness
                           guarantee)
      complexity: O(1) per counterexample
                           construction (constant-size
                           caller state); O(1) per
                           alternative-path classification
                           (3 paths total); O(1) per
                           negative-pin comparison
                           (structural inequality)
      determinism: deterministic; counterexample
                           construction is a pure
                           function of TF-3 + TF-2 alias
                           semantics; alternative-path
                           enumeration is a closed set of
                           3 paths; negative pin is a
                           structural inequality holding
                           across all compilation runs
      reference impl: former IC-8 rule REMOVED from
                           compiler/ori_arc/
                           src/aims/interprocedural/mod.rs
                           (no surviving derivation code);
                           sound paths implemented via
                           IC-2 (`init_optimistic`) + IC-3
                           (`ParamContract::join`) +
                           TF-3 (`Construct` transfer in
                           aims/transfer/) + TF-9 / TF-9a
                           (`Reuse` / `CollectionReuse`
                           transfer); companion DP-10
                           REMOVED from sec-4 truth tables
      cross-language Koka Perceus
      prior art: (`koka/src/Core/CheckFBIP.hs`)
                           derives uniqueness exclusively
                           through monotone fixpoint, never
                           through backward-demand
                           inference — matches the IC-8
                           removal discipline; Lean 4
                           `lean4/src/Lean/Compiler/IR/`
                           uses similar SCC-topological
                           monotone iteration without
                           parallel backward-demand
                           derivation; FP² (Lorenzen et al.
                           ICFP 2023) Section 5 formalizes
                           the uniqueness-as-PAST-RC
                           semantics that the IC-8 removal
                           preserves; arc.md §Reference
                           Repos cites Lean 4 + Swift ARC
                           + Koka Perceus as the prior art
                           set

    Engines dispatched:
      fixpoint (PRIMARY — IC-8-REMOVED soundness via
        constructive counterexample + alternative-paths
        enumeration + negative pin against the former rule's
        output; verifier checks the three conjuncts
        (P1)..(P3) plus side-conditions:
          - (P1) counterexample existence via c_counter
            construction (caller-side Construct + Let Var
            alias both live at call site)
          - (P2) alternative-paths enumeration over the
            3-path set (IC-2/IC-3 SCC fixpoint via fresh
            origin, caller-side TF-3 FRESH, caller-side
            TF-9 / TF-9a Reuse)
          - (P3) negative pin via structural inequality
            between former_IC8_output (Unique) and
            sound_IC_2_IC_3_output (MaybeShared) on
            c_counter
        emits Fail on any divergence)
      interprocedural_summary (per-function callee
        parameter uniqueness derivation routes exclusively
        through IC-2 + IC-3 SCC fixpoint post-IC-8 removal;
        consumed by Step 5 emission to drive DP-4 cow_mode
        + DP-5 can_mutate_in_place gating; consumed by
        RL-29 / RL-30 LLVM fact-export gates)
